Z||000000||Styles||06-06-2000||12:22 AM||||I have an 85 pontiac se. My car will not start it will turn over but not start? Thought it was the fuel pump so I changed it.Nope still no start I am not getting any spark to the plugs tested the pick up and the distributor module and even changed the coil and it still will not start.If any one could help me please help me out||||reg||1
Z||000001||86SE||06-06-2000||01:25 AM||||Are the ignition componets new, or wet?||||reg||1
Z||000002||86SE||06-06-2000||01:27 AM||||how about the starter??  Does it turn over slow?||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||06-06-2000||02:13 AM||||take the distributor cap off and have someone crank it and see if the roter turns -- you can also take the oil filler cap off and see if the lifters are moving -- if either (or both) of those fail it could be a timing gear or a broken timing chain........or even a broken camshaft........in any of those cases you will hear the starter.........||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||06-06-2000||02:29 AM||||If it is a V-6, Pull distributor, Dis-assemble and replace the pick-up coil. Takes about 20 minutes to change out. I have seen this problem many times with V-6's. Just remember how the distributor comes out so you can put it back (where the rotor points to)That will get the timing close enough to run the engine so you can set timing exact.<BR>If you go to this website you can read the entire procedure on how to do it step by step.<BR> <BR> <A HREF="http://home.xnet.com/~nife/articles/tt-pickupcoil.html" TARGET=_blank>http://home.xnet.com/~nife/articles/tt-pickupcoil.html</A> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 06-06-2000).]||||reg||1
